[6.368331, "o", "52m\u001b[1;44H ▐▛███▜▌   Claude Code v2.1.220\u001b[39m\u001b[52X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[2;44H▝▜█████▛▘  Opus 5 (1M context) · API Usage Billing\u001b[39m\u001b[33X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[3;44H  ▘▘ ▝▝    /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/projects/railmux\u001b[39m\u001b[25X\u001b[4;44H\u001b[83X\u001b[38;5;147m\n❯\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252mIn railmux ssh, explain how a mouse-wheel event over an agent pane is served\u001b[39m\u001b[5X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[6;44H  from the fast client's local history overlay rather than forwarded upstream.\u001b[39m\u001b[5X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[7;44H  Point to the exact implementation symbols and one existing focused test that\u001b[39m\u001b[5X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[8;44H  directly asserts empty forwarded_input. Then suggest one small additional\u001b[39m\u001b[8X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[9;44H  assertion.\u001b[39m\u001b[71X\u001b[10;44H\u001b[83X\u001b[38;5;147m\n●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1mTrace SSH wheel ownership\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[56X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[12;44H  railmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[11X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[13;44H  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[17X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[14;44H  LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[58X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[15;44H  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[16;44H  _HistoryViewport.offset and returns HistoryAction with render_history=True and\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[17;44H  forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[41X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[18;44H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set;\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2X\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[19;44H  empty means nothing reaches tmux. The overlay is painted